      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "This required SourceProvider callback is an error guard: the fixture\n supplies cached snapshots by overriding parse. Structural search must\n use those snapshots without refetching. Calling read would fail the\n contract tested below; primitive reads are exercised by other providers."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation sits on a function with a body, `impl[CachedParse/SourceProvider]/fn[read]`. It is in fenced citation commentary, so the explanation counts as tracked. The reason is substantive and matches the current source:\n- `read` is a required trait callback that always returns `SourceError::Invalid(\"cached parser must not refetch\")`.\n- The sibling `parse` override in the same impl returns cached snapshots built with `parse_snapshot`, and it never calls `read`.\n- Zero execution of `read` is therefore the intended outcome of the fixture. If structural search refetched a resource, it would fail.\n- The test `structural_search_uses_overridden_parses_their_snapshot_and_requested_scope` exercises this contract. I did not read its assertions in full, but its setup uses `CachedParse` and `search_structure` with expected match counts.\n- The commentary also says primitive reads are covered by other providers. That is a reasonable pointer, and the claim does not conflict with this code.",
